	(text "16-bit SRAM, 4 x 4 array of 6T cells (PU = PMOS pull-up, PD = NMOS pull-down, PG = NMOS access)\nRead: precharge BLc and BLcB to VDD, raise WLr; the '0' side discharges its bit line through PG + PD,\n      a sense amplifier resolves the BL - BLB difference.\nWrite: drive BLc / BLcB to the data and its complement, raise WLr; PG pulls the '1' node low and flips the cell.\nSizing (W/L): PD 3 > PG 1.5 > PU 1\n  cell ratio CR = PD / PG = 3 / 1.5 = 2 (read stability: '0' node stays below the trip point)\n  pull-up ratio PR = PU / PG = 1 / 1.5 = 0.67 (writability: PG overpowers PU)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 78.74 203.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
